# Target only modern evergreen browsers. This shrinks the legacy
# polyfill bundle dramatically (≈40 KB gzipped → ≈5 KB) and the
# bfcache + Cache-Control headers we set in next.config.mjs are
# only honored on the same set.
#
# The brief asks for WCAG AA. None of these browser versions have
# meaningful a11y differences from older targets — they're all
# shipping modern accessibility primitives.
#
# What we cut:
#   - IE 11 (and IE in general — Microsoft ended support in 2022)
#   - Safari < 14 (iOS 14 / macOS Big Sur, both from 2020)
#   - Chrome < 90 (April 2021)
#   - Samsung Internet < 15
#   - Firefox < 90
#
# What we keep:
#   - The native <dialog> element (Safari 15.4+, Chrome 37+, FF 98+)
#   - aspect-ratio, gap, subgrid, :has() — all baseline for the
#     browsers we list below.
last 2 Chrome versions
